            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous multivessel coronary vasospasm documented by coronary arteriography. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>434-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of spontaneous multivessel coronary artery spasm documented by coronary arteriography is reported. The patient was also resistant to sublingual nitrates and nifedipine and required intracoronary nitroglycerine to alleviate the spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
